From bfb916015946940b71b328019e5c1f767bf0ce71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Louvignes <olivier@mgcrea.io>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 07:59:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/40] mfd: axp20x: add the AXP2101

The AXP2101 is an X-Powers PMIC with five DC-DC converters, eleven LDOs,
a charger and a fuel gauge, used on the HiBy R1 among others. Add it to
the axp20x core with its register map and interrupts, and cells for the
regulators, the USB power supply and the battery charger. It powers off
through bit 0 of COMM_CFG (0x10), not AXP20X_OFF_CTRL.

The register map comes from the GPL driver HiBy's firmware uses and was
checked against the chip's state on a running R1.
---
 drivers/mfd/axp20x-i2c.c   |   2 +
 drivers/mfd/axp20x.c       | 107 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 include/linux/mfd/axp20x.h | 114 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 221 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/axp20x-i2c.c b/drivers/mfd/axp20x-i2c.c
